 (18, "The ratio was almost exactly one foot of fall for every thousand feet of distance.", "The river fell about one foot in every hundred and sixteen, a torrent’s slope, far too steep for a channel that meant to keep its banks."),
 (18, "That’s the gradient for a canal that stays put.", "That’s the gradient for a race that stays put, so we make the water walk the long way round and keep the fall for the wheel."),
